# Documentation (normative)

**Before creating or editing docs or agent configuration, read:**

[`docs/specs/documentation-spec.md`](../../docs/specs/documentation-spec.md)

## Document types

| Type | Path | For agents |
|------|------|------------|
| **Specs** | `docs/specs/` | Yes — normative |
| **Reference** | `docs/reference/` | No — humans only |
| **Plans** | `docs/sprints/` | No — lifecycle trackers |

## Must follow

1. **One concern per spec** — self-contained; no links to other documents.
2. **`AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules/`** — index specs only; never link reference or plans.
3. **Architecture changes** — update the relevant spec in the same PR as code.
4. **Progress / gaps** — reference docs or plans only; never specs.
5. **Portal authorization** — backend grant/seed changes: verify portal actor labels in webapp and graceful 403 degradation.

## Cursor rules

One rule file per spec in `.cursor/rules/` — each points to exactly one spec in `docs/specs/`.
